  "final_message": "I haven't changed anything yet. The repo shows that something still reads `channel`, and removing it would break a consumer.\n\n**The conflict:** `contracts/consumers/analytics-ingest__OrderPlaced.json` is the contract for analytics-ingest. It lists `deployedVersion: 3`, and its `requires` includes:\n\n```json\n\"channel\": \"enum:web|store|marketplace\"\n```\n\n`npm run contracts` (`scripts/verify-contracts.mjs`) checks every consumer contract against the events the service actually publishes. If I remove `channel` from `OrderPlaced`, the check fails with `ARCH-4 FAIL analytics-ingest: OrderPlaced.channel missing`. More importantly, it would probably break analytics-ingest in production if it still parses that field. The billing-service and OrderCancelled contracts don't use `channel`, so analytics-ingest is the only one blocking this.\n\n**What the removal would touch:**\n- `src/core/events.ts:16,50`: the event field and the mapping that fills it\n- `src/core/order.ts:23,35,75,124-125`: the field in the model and input types, plus its validation (`CHANNELS`/`Channel` might then be unused)\n- `src/api/requestParsing.ts:18,39-40`: reading `channel` from the request\n- Tests: `test/app.test.ts`, `test/order.test.ts` (including the validation-paths assertion), `test/helpers.ts`, `test/adapters.test.ts`\n- `scripts/verify-contracts.mjs` sample order, `README.md` and `CLAUDE.md` examples\n\n**How do you want to proceed?**\n1. **Analytics-ingest has already stopped using it.** If so, their contract is out of date and should be updated first, ideally by that team publishing a new version without `channel`. Once it's updated, I'll do the full removal.\n2. **Remove it from the order model and API only, and keep it on the event.** This doesn't really work, because the event gets `channel` from the order. I'd have to add a placeholder value, which would send analytics bad data.\n3. **Hold off** until you've confirmed with the analytics-ingest owners.\n\nIf you can confirm option 1, should I also edit `analytics-ingest__OrderPlaced.json` here, or will that update come from their side?",
